From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] applet: wait longer for the panel connection

The daemon gave the panel 1 s to connect over the private socket that
cosmic-session hands both of them. A panel that is slow to start (cold
start from a USB stick, first-boot load) missed it: the daemon moved on,
the panel then failed "to connect to the notifications daemon" and never
started its applets -- an empty desktop with no panel or dock. See
pop-os/cosmic-panel#635; #404 raised the panel-side timeout only.

Upstream: not submitted
---
diff --git a/src/subscriptions/applet.rs b/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
index 56bd9bd..55d97ae 100644
--- a/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
+++ b/src/subscriptions/applet.rs
@@ -18,8 +18,11 @@ use std::os::unix::io::FromRawFd;
 pub async fn setup_panel_conn(tx: Sender<Input>) -> Result<Connection> {
     let socket = setup_panel_socket()?;
     let guid = Guid::generate();
+    // Wait for the panel as long as it may take to start: with 1 s, a panel
+    // slow to come up (cold start from USB, first-boot load) missed the
+    // handshake, and without it the panel never started its applets.
     let conn = tokio::time::timeout(
-        tokio::time::Duration::from_secs(1),
+        tokio::time::Duration::from_secs(30),
         Builder::socket(socket)
             .p2p()
             .server(guid)
